# Run 115 auto-queue daily cap — GREEN evidence (after review repair)

date: 2026-11-01
contract: replay.auto_queue is in the unified runtime config readback, defaults to
enabled=true/daily_cap=100, accepts PUT patches, and maps onto a hard replay ledger daily
counterfactual ceiling that binds on every channel and on the admission availability check.

## Path resolution (HOLD 1)
resolveAutoQueueConfigPath mirrors the host: explicit --unified-runtime-config first, then
<runtimeStateRoot>/runtime-config.yaml, then legacy <runtimeStateRoot>/state/runtime-config.yaml.
The CLI resolver receives options.unifiedRuntimeConfigPath and is exported for resolver-level tests.

## Disabled/cap enforcement (HOLD 2)
applyAutoQueueDailyCap sets hardCounterfactualLimit alongside counterfactualsPerDay. The ledger
checks the hard ceiling before the channel-scoped enforced guard, so enabled:false (0) refuses on
development/stage too. replayBudgetAvailable now returns false when the hard ceiling is spent,
including hard 0 under enforced:false, so upper layers do not attempt a reservation that must fail.

